---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "adhd & pattern recognition — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>adhd & pattern recognition</h1>
    <p>adhd brains are often exceptional pattern-recognizers. you notice when things don't match the expected pattern, you spot similarities across domains, you see what others miss. this is a superpower in fields like data analysis, creative work, and debugging. the trade-off: you may struggle to stay on the pattern others have decided matters.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>notice your pattern-spotting: what kinds of patterns do you naturally see?</li>
      <li>leverage this in work: analysis roles, creative roles, exploratory roles suit you</li>
      <li>communicate your pattern-spotting to others; it's not obvious to them</li>
      <li>watch for false patterns (your brain will sometimes see patterns that aren't there)</li>
      <li>use pattern-spotting to understand yourself: notice your own cycles, rhythms, triggers</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="care">pattern recognition is powerful but can be exhausting. give yourself permission to ignore patterns sometimes.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
